{
 "board": "bolt-earring",
 "note": "The bolt earring (compose.json) as blocks and loose connections. The pin solver picks the RP2350's pins for the IMU's I2C and interrupt, the charger's two status lines, the power latch's hold and button lines, the two dividers and the light sensor (ADC inputs), and each LED zone's switch enable and data. The rest is wired by hand: power, USB (its pins are fixed), BOOTSEL and RUN from the long-press block, the SWD test points, and each zone's rail and first data line. The zone switches' enables pass the level check because their ON input draws at most 1 uA, at which an RP2350 pin's low is far below the switch's 0.4 V VIL (the datasheet's 0.5 V VOL is at 2 mA).",
 "instances": {
